          %title
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#commonfurtherassumptions"} Common further assumptions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#frobenius_system"} Frobenius system
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#vertical_tangent_lie_algebroid"} vertical tangent Lie algebroid
              %li
                %a{:href => "#systems_of_partial_differential_equations"} systems of partial differential equations
          %h1#idea Idea
          %p There are several different ways to think about differential systems:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} general abstract way
                which we shall put forward here:
              %p
                an exterior differential system is a sub-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie-∞-algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a} \hookrightarrow T X
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                that is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
                of a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝔧
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : T X \to \mathfrak{j}
                of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie-∞-algebroids
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %mi ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi p
                      %mi 𝔧
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathfrak{a} := ker(p) \hookrightarrow T X \stackrel{p}{\to}
                      \\mathfrak{j}
            %li
              %p
                In the literature – the the
                %a{:href => "#references"} references
                below – the term
                %em exterior differential system
                is instead introduced and understood in the context of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+algebra"} dg-algebra
                as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset \Omega^\bullet(X)
                inside the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deRham+dg-algebra"} deRham dg-algebra
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and all concepts there are developed from this perspective.
              %p
                From this the above perspective is obtained by noticing that from a dg-ideal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                we are naturally led to form the quotient
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)/J
                which is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
                of the inclusion
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mo *
                        %mo :
                        %mi J
                        %mo ↪
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^* : J \hookrightarrow \Omega^\bullet(X)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mover
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi coker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi J
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      J \stackrel{p^*}{\hookrightarrow} \Omega^\bullet(X) \to coker(p^*) =
                      \\Omega^\bullet(X)/J
                      \\,.
              %p
                The existing literature on exterior differential systems is actually a bit unclear about which
                %a{:href => "#commonfurtherassumptions"} additional assumptions
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                are supposed to be a crucial part of the definition. However, in most applications of interest — see the
                %a{:href => "#examples"} examples
                below — it turns out that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                is in fact a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
                (over
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
              %p Here we take this as indication that
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    it makes good sense to understand exterior differential systems in the restricted sense where the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                    is required to be a
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
                %li
                  %p
                    the reason that the existing literature does present the desired extra assumptions on the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                    in an incoherent fashion is due to a lack of global structural insight into the role of the definition of exterior differential systems.
              %p
                Because, recall that a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie-∞-algebroid
                is – effectively by definition – the formal dual of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree
                = succeed "-graded" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                all
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie-∞-algebroids
                and then the above
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
                sequence of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
                sequence of
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie-∞-algebroid
            %li
              %p
                Historically, one can trace back the basic idea of exterior differential systems to
                = succeed "\u2018s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eli+Cartan"} Eli Cartan
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+differential+equation"} partial differential equation
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
              %p for each system of partial differential equations
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi F
                        %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi μ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mi μ
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mi ρ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\{
                      F^\rho(\{x^\mu\}_{\mu}, \{f^j\}_j, \{\frac{\partial f^j}{\partial x^\mu}\} ) = 0
                      \\}_\rho
              %p
                there is a space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \in \Omega^\bullet(X)
                such that solutions of the system of equations are given by
                %strong integral manifolds
                of the exterior differential system determined by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            The notion of an integral manifold of an exterior differential system is crucial in the theory: in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            it is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to X
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^* J = 0
          %p
            But this says precisely that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            extends to morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie-∞-algebroids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi : T \Sigma \to \mathfrak{a}
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{a}) = \Omega^\bullet(X)/J
            as above. Therefore the relevance of the notion of
            %em integral manifolds
            in the theory we take as another indication that exterior differential systems are usefully thought of as being about
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie-∞-algebroids
          %h1#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_exterior_differential_system Definition (exterior differential system)
            %p
              An
              %strong exterior differential system
              on a smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset \Omega^\bullet(X)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deRham+dg-algebra"} deRham dg-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            being a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
            means explicitly that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\forall \theta\in J \subset \Omega^\bullet(X), \omega \in \Omega^\bullet(X):
                      \\theta \wedge \omega \in J
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-grading" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = \oplus_{k \in \mathbb{N}} J_k
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                is induced from that of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)
                in that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mi J
                      %mo ∩
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_k = J \cap \Omega^\bullet(k)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi d
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall \theta \in J \subset \Omega^\bullet(X) : d \theta \in J
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong integral manifold
              of an exterior differential system is a submanifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : Y \hookrightarrow X
              such that the restriction of all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \in J
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              vanishes:
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} that
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi Y
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \that|_Y = 0
          %p
            In other words, for an integral manifold the pullback of the ideal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            along the inclusion map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            vanishes:
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo *
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^* J = 0
          %h2#commonfurtherassumptions Common further assumptions
          %p Often further assumptions are imposed on exterior differential systems. Here are some:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An exterior differential system is called
                %strong finitely generated
                if there is a finite set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta_k \in \Omega^\bullet(X)\}
                of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
                generated by these, so that
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi j
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi j
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      J = \{ \sum_i f_i \theta_i  + \sum_j g_j d \theta_j| f_i, g_j \in C^\infty(X)\}
                      \\,.
            %li
              %p
                Often it is assumed that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %mi ℝ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_0 = \mathbb{R}
              %p
                Dually in terms of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroids"} Lie-∞-algebroids
                this assumption means that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie-∞-algebroid
                that is just an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebra"} L-∞-algebra
            %li
              .num_defn
                %h6#definition_strict_independence_condition Definition (strict independence condition)
                %p
                  A
                  %strong strict independence condition
                  on an exterior differential system
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset \Omega^\bullet(X)
                  is an
                  = succeed "-form" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^n(X)
                  for some
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  such that
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                      is decomposable into a wedge product of
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      1-forms mod
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi J
                              %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^n
                  %li
                    %p
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                      is pointwise not an element of
                      = succeed "." do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi J
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \omega)
                  am exterior differential system with strict independence condition
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ω
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                  %strong integral manifold
                  is now more restrictively an integral manifold
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo :
                        %mi Σ
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : \Sigma \to X
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  but now such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo *
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^* \omega
                  is a volume form on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                  (i.e. pointwise non-vanishing).
          %h1#special_cases special cases
          %p Some special types of exterior differential systems carry their own names.
          %h2#frobenius_system Frobenius system
          %p
            A
            %strong Frobenius system
            is an exterior differential system
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset \Omega^\bullet(X)
            that is locally generated as a graded-commutative algebra from a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi j
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta_j \in \Omega^1(U)\}_j
            of 1-forms.
          %p
            Frobenius systems are in bijection with involutive subbundles of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \hookrightarrow T X
            such that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v,w \in \Gamma(E) \subset \Gamma(T X)
            also the Lie bracket of vector fields of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            lands in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [v,w] \in \Gamma(E) \subset \Gamma(T X)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                given a Frobenius system the sections of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(E)
                are defined locally to be the joint
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
                of the maps
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi θ
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta_i : \Gamma(T U) \to \mathbb{R}\}
            %li
              %p
                given ab involutive subbundle
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                the corresponding Frobenius system is the collection of 1-forms that vanishes on
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi θ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi θ
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = \{\theta \in \Omega^1(X) | \theta|_{E} = 0\}
                \.
          %p
            Notice that the involutive subbundle may be thought of precisely as a sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  E &amp;&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;&amp; T X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  }
          %p
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
            (i.e. as a sub
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-%E2%88%9E-algebroid"} Lie-∞-algebroid
            that happens to be an ordinary
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is the quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(X)/J
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deRham+dg-algebra"} deRham dg-algebra
            by the Frobenius system:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi J
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(E) = \Omega^\bullet(X)/J
                  \\,.
          %h3#vertical_tangent_lie_algebroid vertical tangent Lie algebroid
          %p
            A special case of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            corresponding to a Frobenius system is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+tangent+Lie+algebroid"} vertical tangent Lie algebroid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi vert
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_{vert} Y
            of a map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi : Y \to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi T
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(\pi_*) \subset T Y
            of vertical vector fields on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            %strong horizontal differential forms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi hor
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi ω
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  J = \Omega^\bullet_{hor}(Y) = \{\omega \in \Omega^1(Y)| \forall v \in ker(\pi_*): \omega(v) = 0\}
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi vert
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi hor
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  CE(T_{vert} Y) = \Omega^\bullet(Y)/\Omega^\bullet_{hor}(Y)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            of
            %strong vertical differential forms
            with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %p
            This plays a central role in the theory of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann+connection"} Ehresmann connection
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cartan-Ehresmann+%E2%88%9E-connection"} Cartan-Ehresmann ∞-connection
          %h2#systems_of_partial_differential_equations systems of partial differential equations
          %p A system
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi s
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi s
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{
                  F^\rho : \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^s \times \mathbb{R}^{n \cdot s}
                  \\to
                  \\mathbb{R}
                  \\}_\rho
          %p
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+differential+equation"} partial differential equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi μ
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x^\mu\}_{\mu = 1}^n
            and functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f^i\}_{i = 1}^s
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi x
                          %mi μ
                    %mo )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{
                  F^\rho((x^\mu), (f^i), \left(\frac{\partial f^i}{\partial x^\mu}\right))
                  \= 0
                  \\}
          %p is encoded by an exterior differential system on the 0-locus
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi s
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ∀
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi ρ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X := \{(x,f,p) \in \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{R}^s \times \mathbb{R}^{n s} |
                  \\forall \rho : F^\rho(x,f,p) = 0 \}
          %p
            of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi ρ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi ρ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{F^\rho\}_\rho
            (assuming that this is a manifold) with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-ideal"} dg-ideal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = \langle \theta_i \rangle_i
            generated by the 1-forms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi θ
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi i
                  %mo −
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msubsup
                    %mi p
                    %mi μ
                    %mi i
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi μ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta^i := d f^i - \sum_{\mu=1}^n p^i_\mu d x^\mu
                  \\,.
          %p
            Namely a solution to the system of partial differential equations is precisely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the projection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \to \mathbb{R}^n
          %p which defined an integral manifold of the exterior differential system.
          %h1#references References
          %p The standard textbook is
          %ul
            %li
              Bryant et al.,
              %em Exterior differential systems
          %p Course note are provided in
          %ul
            %li
              Bryant,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/EDS-notes.pdf", :title => "Notes on Exterior Differential Systems"} Notes on Exterior Differential Systems
